## Overview

**M.O.B. (Motors on Boost)** is an aggressive arcade highway racing baseline inspired by legendary mid-2000s classics—principally *Need for Speed: Most Wanted (2005)* and *Burnout Revenge (2005)*. 

Engineered directly on top of Haxe 4.3+ and the Heaps.io framework, **M.O.B.** runs natively in modern Chromium, Gecko, and WebKit browsers via hardware-accelerated WebGL 2.0. The engine combines custom raycast vehicle dynamics, high-speed lateral drift modeling, procedural endless multi-lane highway track generation, autonomous highway traffic AI, dynamic trauma-based camera shake, and a built-in Web Audio procedural tone synthesizer into an installable Progressive Web Application (PWA).

This project represents the primary WebGL foundation of the *M.O.B.* racing line, setting the architectural foundation for upcoming sister iterations (such as the planned Godot-powered desktop title, *M.O.B. // Sektr*).

---

## Key Features

* **Arcade Vehicle Handling**: Custom suspension physics with raycast ground clamping, steering rack smoothing, tire slip curves, dynamic counter-steering drift logic, and high-velocity nitrous acceleration.
* **Trauma-Based Chase Camera**: Spring-arm third-person chase camera featuring velocity-aligned look-ahead, speed-dependent FOV stretching, and non-linear rotational camera trauma triggered by drift snaps, nitro boost, and near-misses.
* **Autonomous Highway Traffic AI**: Multi-lane procedural obstacle vehicles traversing route waypoints with dynamic spatial proximity checks, lane-following, and collision boundaries.
* **Cinematic 3-Stage Boot Sequence**:
  1. **Studio Splash**: Developer and publisher branding with smooth alpha curves (`intro/jagofr-rvl-splash.webp`).
  2. **Engine Splash**: Heaps.io and Haxe engine recognition (`intro/heaps-haxe-splash.webp`).
  3. **Locked Preload & Disclaimer**: Mandatory legal, health, and open-source acknowledgments acting as an asynchronous background loading barrier with aligned attribution logos.
  4. **Showcase Cross-Fade**: A 1.2-second smooth curtain cross-fade transitioning directly to the rotating 3D vehicle showcase and pulsating splash screen.
* **Procedural Vector Iconography (`UIIcons.hx`)**: Resolution-independent vector UI symbols drawn on the fly via `h2d.Graphics` and cached into `h2d.Tile` textures, bypassing TrueType variable-font rasterization limitations.
* **Bumper-Navigated Glassmorphic UI**: High-contrast UI featuring edge-triggered bumper/tab navigation (`LB`/`RB` or `Q`/`E`), discrete block audio volume gauges (`■` / `□`), and real-time graphics adjustments.
* **Dual-Scheme Hardware Diagrams**: Procedural vector controller diagrams (PXN P50L / standard Xbox layouts) and keyboard diagrams with in-game button remapping and device isolation modes (`Both`, `Keyboard Only`, `Gamepad Only`).
* **Web Audio Synthesis Engine**: Custom square, sawtooth, and noise tone generators producing procedural engine RPM frequency modulation, tire screeches, and UI chime sound effects without external audio files.
* **State Persistence**: Browser `LocalStorage` caching for hardware graphics levels, audio channels, and mid-run race checkpoints.

---

## Architecture & Systems

```
                              ┌────────────────────────┐
                              │        Main.hx         │
                              │  (Boot & State Machine) │
                              └───────────┬────────────┘
                                          │
            ┌─────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┐
            ▼                             ▼                            ▼
  ┌───────────────────┐         ┌───────────────────┐        ┌───────────────────┐
  │   IntroSequence   │         │    Physics & 3D   │        │     UI & Audio    │
  ├───────────────────┤         ├───────────────────┤        ├───────────────────┤
  │ • Studio Splash   │         │ • CarPhysics.hx   │        │ • UIManager.hx    │
  │ • Engine Splash   │         │ • Track.hx        │        │ • UIIcons.hx      │
  │ • Disclaimer/FOSS │         │ • TrafficSystem.hx│        │ • ControlDiagrams │
  │ • Async Preload   │         │ • ChaseCamera.hx  │        │ • AudioManager.hx │
  │ • Showcase Curtain│         │ • GraphicsManager │        │ • SaveSystem.hx   │
  └───────────────────┘         └───────────────────┘        └───────────────────┘
```

### Module Breakdown

| Module | Location | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| **Entry Point** | `src/Main.hx` | Boot state machine, canvas resize lifecycle, showcase rotation, and async asset loading. |
| **Physics** | `src/physics/CarPhysics.hx` | Velocity integration, lateral tire slip friction, chassis roll/pitch, and drift transitions. |
| **World** | `src/world/Track.hx` | Procedural multi-lane spline road generation, asphalt shaders, and ground lift constants. |
| **Traffic** | `src/entities/TrafficSystem.hx` | Autonomous obstacle spawning, waypoint trajectory math, and collision volumes. |
| **Vehicle Mesh** | `src/entities/CarMesh.hx` | Procedural 3D chassis geometry, materials, and steerable front wheel assemblies. |
| **Camera** | `src/core/ChaseCamera.hx` | Damped spring chase camera with dynamic FOV dilation and non-linear trauma shake decay. |
| **UI Management** | `src/core/UIManager.hx` | Menus, sliders, credits view, bumper tab navigation, and modal containment. |
| **Vector Icons** | `src/core/UIIcons.hx` | Procedural vector icon generation via `h2d.Graphics` cached to `h2d.Tile`. |
| **Input Handler** | `src/input/InputController.hx` | Edge-detection polling for Gamepad API and keyboard with remapping registers. |
| **Audio Synth** | `src/core/AudioManager.hx` | Web Audio tone synthesis for engine frequencies, tire friction, and UI beeps. |
| **Persistence** | `src/core/SaveSystem.hx` | Serialization of graphics settings, audio gains, and in-progress race saves. |

